00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.350
Uh on the right I've an

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.790
eight-bit um

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.510
counting in binary. So, the only input

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.590
to this system it's a synchronous system

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.710
is the clock. We change from one state

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.310
to another. And since the output is just

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:30.870
a binary sequence, I've just written the

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.150
binary sequence into each state.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.510
Obviously, we want to deal with uh

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.830
things that respond to input signals.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.190
So, we need uh to have branches, a

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.550
decision and so we have what's called a

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.950
decision box. So, at the output of the

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.150
