00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.630
expression. So, we have some sort of

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.350
expression in there,

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.670
which is either true or false.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.310
Uh if it's true, we go to one exit path,

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.470
and if it's false, we go to a different

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.350
one.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.790
So, a decision box constructs

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:06.270
conditional next state. This next state

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.910
is now a function of the current state

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:11.230
and the inputs. The outputs are still

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.990
just listed in the state box.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.390
Okay, so this correspond to all we need

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.870
for a Mealy model,

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.990
as it happens. Typically, the exit path

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.790
is determined by the input on the next

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.950
clock edge. Like that's that's basically

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.150
what uh is going to happen.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.230
As I said, but just be careful. You only

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.190
ever have one entry path, and that

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.909
always goes in to the top of the state

00:06:32.919 --> 00:06:35.310
box.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:36.710
So, as I said, this is sequential

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.190
machines which generate state outputs,

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.390
Mealy model type state machines.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.070
The final element that we need, so we

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.030
only really need three elements,

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.070
is we need some mechanism to uh

